  "story": {
    "day": 95,
    "title": "Kaya's Busy Saturday",
    "sentences": [
      "It was a cool Saturday in late autumn; Kaya loved her life.",
      "She went to the library and sat in a chair.",
      "On the chalk board, \"Music Club at eleven\" was written.",
      "Her band would sing a new song.",
      "Kaya had to write lyrics and was ready, one hundred percent sure.",
      "She could not change the order of songs.",
      "She saw the track and field but did not swim in the pool.",
      "Instead, she practiced guitar for six hours.",
      "Practice ended at seven. Then, eight friends met at a restaurant.",
      "Kaya watched for her salad, bread, and chocolate.",
      "Her empty plate made her smile. It felt like December.",
      "\"Whose turn is it at ten?\" she asked, remembering a witch book."
    ]
  }
}